# tools/entry_names.allow -- the sites tools/entry_names_check.rb lets name an entry by hand.
# CLASS<TAB>file<TAB>function<TAB>pattern<TAB>count<TAB>why no String kind can name a deleted bytes entry here
# A site is keyed by its function and its pattern, not by its text; the count is how many times the pattern occurs
# in the function, and a copy of a listed line changes it. CLASS (several join with +):
#   NUM   an Int or Float container: the entry named has no String form
#   POLY  the container holds boxed (Poly) values
#   ARM   a String kind takes the _e arm before this one; this arm is the other kinds
#   ROW   the suffix is the container row's, formatted at the site and not routed through emit_elem_entry
#   READ  the operation is a read or an aggregate, not a store or a search
#   IDX   deletes by index: no String value enters

